*Observations.* $\#S(H)$ for all 22 cycle types matches Smith's Lemma 1. $sum_T P(T)(1-(3\/4)^(\#S(H))) = 0.185738$ reproduces Smith's 18.57% (eq. (12)), where $3\/4$ comes from his Hypotheses 2–3. Without those hypotheses, the rational-tractable fraction is 0.50159. On every curve, $chi_pi mod 2$ equals the characteristic polynomial of the root permutation on $J[2]$ (0 mismatches). *The class closure equals the direct fraction for every $p$.*

*Derived.* On $S_8$, $chi mod 2$ determines whether a tractable subgroup exists (finite check, table below). It is an isogeny invariant, so a walk inside the hyperelliptic locus never creates a tractable subgroup. It can only flip Smith's square conditions (Props. 2, 4); under his hypotheses this bounds the gain at 18.57% → 50.16%. That is open (`problems/smith-kernel-isogeny-class-walk.md`).
