= Where the leads meet
#figure(image("/figures/pipeline_status.svg", width: 100%), caption: [Status of each step of the proposed pipeline.])
The pipeline does not compose as stated. GHS lands over $FF_(2^l)$, and Smith's trigonal construction "does not apply in characteristics 2 and 3" (Smith 2009). A derived reason: an ordinary genus-3 Jacobian in characteristic 2 has $\#J[2](overline(k)) = 2^3$. See `problems/ghs-to-smith-pipeline-characteristic-mismatch.md`. The end-to-end proportion is not computable from this study.

